<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 40,021 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 40,021 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 40,021 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 92,665 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 2,075	    4,892</p>
<p>    Import cargo			37,946	   87,773</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours seven ships were expected to sail and 13 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Feul oil		 26,000	 Zanjan		24/9</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,000	 Yin Chuan	    due</p>
<p>Fertilizer	     29,700	 Visvliet	    24/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		 13,000	 Bunga Angarik     23/9</p>
<p>Motor gasoline	 26,200	 Iter		  22/9</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Santa Lucia	 21/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		  8,000	 Strength	    21/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
